text:
maria: Hi all — split the original giant PR into three focused commits per feedback. Addressed the inline comments about edge-case handling and renamed RetryPolicy -> BackoffPolicy. Ran unit tests locally. PTAL when you have a moment. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/repo/pull/1234

alex: Quick skim — much cleaner now, thanks. Two small asks: 1) add a null-check in the request handler, 2) add a debug log when backoff increases. Also the commit message for the second commit could be clearer.

maria: Thanks — added the null-check and the debug log, and updated the commit message. Force-pushed to the branch. Snippet I added:
```ts
if (!req.user) {
  return res.status(400).json({ error: 'missing user' });
}
logger.debug('backoff.increase', { id: req.id, newDelayMs: delay });
```

ci-bot: CI: all checks passed on latest push ✅ (lint, unit, integration)

julian: Looks good from my side. One more request: can you add a tiny unit test for the backoff increase path so we don't regress? Should be quick.

maria: Good call — added `backoff.test.ts` with a mocked timer. Test snippet:
```ts
it('increments backoff on transient failures', async () => {
  jest.useFakeTimers();
  const result = await sendWithBackoff(mockReq);
  jest.runAllTimers();
  expect(result.retries).toBeGreaterThan(0);
});
```
Pushed again.

sam: Nice, the test looks sensible and small. Also the structured log makes it easier to search — approving from my side. :thumbsup:

tasha: Any concerns about canary timing?

maria: Plan is to merge after one more approval and then start a 10% canary for 30 minutes with monitored error rates. If anything spikes we roll back.

alex: I can give final approve after the test finishes in CI. Thanks for iterating quickly.

maria: thanks everyone — appreciate the quick turnaround.
